@reporter 

Thanks for sharing that and for creating this issue. There has certainly been a regression here. I already have a fix for this issue on the 0.25 branch and can publish a RC build in a few days.

For now, you have to explicitly set `drop_tokens_threshold=X` where `X` is some high number to get the older behavior.

@reporter 

By default Typesense ignores hyphens, so `Saj-Spicy` is indexed as `SajSpicy`. So that is not returned anymore for the `Spicy` query because Typesense does only prefix search and not suffix search. If you want the words to be split on hyphens and indexed as separate words then you have to configure hyphen in the collection schema as a separator this way:

```
 curl -k "http://localhost:8108/collections" -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -H "X-TYPESENSE-API-KEY: ${TYPESENSE_API_KEY}" -d '{
        "name": "coll",
        "fields": [
          {"name": "title", "type": "string" }
        ], 
        "token_separators": ["-"]
      }'
```
